  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Three senior figures within the Indonesian Solidarity Party (PSI)—Giring Ganesha, Raja Juli Antoni, and Isyana Bagoes Oka—have stepped down from their respective party positions. The decision follows their ongoing professional obligations in the administration of President Prabowo Subianto. According to reports, the individuals are relinquishing their party roles to ensure their full attention remains on their ministerial and government responsibilities. PSI leadership, including Chairman Kaesang Pangarep and other DPP officials, has responded to the news by acknowledging the departures and confirming that the resignations were officially processed. The party has characterized these exits as the voluntary exercise of the members' rights, maintaining a neutral stance regarding the impact of these changes on the organization's internal structure. This development represents a significant shift in the party's composition as these members transition fully toward their public executive roles within the current government framework.",
